WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.891
An index keeps its keys sorted, in pages of a fixed size.

2
00:00:06.891 --> 00:00:09.905
In this toy tree a page holds three keys.

3
00:00:09.905 --> 00:00:13.067
A real page of 8 kilobytes holds about 400.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.846
Keys 10, 20 and 30 go into the page in order.

5
00:00:16.846 --> 00:00:18.028
Now it is full.

6
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.738
Key 40 doesn't fit, and a page can't grow.

7
00:00:21.738 --> 00:00:27.921
So the page splits: a new page is made on its right, and the upper half of the keys moves there.

8
00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:31.162
Now a search must know which page to read.

9
00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:37.004
So a new node is made above, holding one separator: 30, the new page's first key.

10
00:00:37.004 --> 00:00:38.302
Below 30, go left.

11
00:00:38.302 --> 00:00:39.744
30 and up, go right.

12
00:00:39.967 --> 00:00:42.131
The 30 is copied up, not moved.

13
00:00:42.131 --> 00:00:45.622
The bottom pages, the leaves, must hold every key.

14
00:00:45.622 --> 00:00:48.136
The node above holds only signposts.

15
00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.847
Keys 50 to 90 arrive.

16
00:00:49.847 --> 00:00:55.911
Each time a leaf is full, it splits the same way, and one more separator is copied up.

17
00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:57.997
Now insert 100.

18
00:00:57.997 --> 00:01:02.040
The last leaf is full, so it splits, and 90 is copied up.

19
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.657
But now the node above has four keys, one too many.

20
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:07.070
So it splits too.

21
00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:13.582
Its middle key, 70, moves up and is not kept below, because up here keys are only signposts.

22
00:01:13.582 --> 00:01:16.980
Nothing is above it, so 70 becomes the new root.

23
00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.378
That is the only way the tree gets taller: a new root on top.

24
00:01:21.378 --> 00:01:27.475
So every leaf is at the same depth, and finding 60 reads one page per level: three pages.

25
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.905
The leaves are linked left to right, which makes ranges cheap.

26
00:01:31.905 --> 00:01:36.652
To read keys 40 to 70, the search goes down once, to the leaf with 40.

27
00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:42.015
Then it walks right along the links, and stops at 80, the first key above 70.

28
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:44.744
A real page holds about 400 keys.

29
00:01:44.744 --> 00:01:51.057
So three levels hold 64 million keys, and any one of them is three page reads away.
